WEBVTT

00:00:12.949 --> 00:00:16.913
Take your brother outside as
fast as you can! Now Dean! Go!

00:00:18.755 --> 00:00:20.558
Mary! No!

00:00:23.082 --> 00:00:24.864
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:27.802
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:27.915 --> 00:00:29.237
Jess excuse us.

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:33.191
I swore I was done hunting,

00:00:33.824 --> 00:00:34.541
For good.

00:00:34.613 --> 00:00:35.484
I can't do this alone.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.665
Now you're taking off the middle of the
night to spend the week-End with them.

00:00:38.666 --> 00:00:41.166
Hey, everything's gonna be OK.

00:00:41.209 --> 00:00:42.479
I promise.

00:00:44.354 --> 00:00:45.768
You think mom would
have wanted this for us?

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:47.716
Dean, we were raised like warriors.

00:00:47.771 --> 00:00:50.855
You have a responsability.
To dad and his cruisade.

00:00:50.988 --> 00:00:54.400
Even if you do find the thing
that killed her, mom's gone

00:00:54.796 --> 00:00:56.966
And she isn't coming back.

00:00:57.503 --> 00:00:59.632
Don't talk about her like that.

00:01:00.778 --> 00:01:01.735
Dad's gone.

00:01:01.796 --> 00:01:03.439
I've got his journal.
He left me a message.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:05.754
It's coordinates he
left us. It's weird, man.

00:01:05.837 --> 00:01:06.431
Hey, Dean,

00:01:06.541 --> 00:01:07.495
What I said earlier,

00:01:07.573 --> 00:01:08.919
I'm sorry.

00:01:09.498 --> 00:01:10.922
No chick-Flick moments.

00:01:12.694 --> 00:01:13.727
Yes.

00:01:23.085 --> 00:01:24.149
No!

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:37.762
We got work to do.

00:02:16.209 --> 00:02:17.629
Dude, you're cheating.

00:02:17.956 --> 00:02:20.126
No, you just suck.

00:02:26.391 --> 00:02:29.433
Hey, Hailey. Day six. We're
still out near Black Water Ridge.

00:02:29.434 --> 00:02:33.434
We're fine, keeping safe, so
don't worry. Talk to you tomorrow.

00:02:42.761 --> 00:02:45.150
Hey, where you going?
My moment of victory.

00:02:45.272 --> 00:02:46.815
Nature calls.

00:03:29.039 --> 00:03:30.022
Brad?

00:03:31.701 --> 00:03:33.316
Gary, what's going on?

00:04:51.235 --> 00:04:53.896
I am, um...

00:04:54.598 --> 00:05:00.030
You always said roses were
lame, so, I brought you, uh...

00:05:14.897 --> 00:05:16.316
Jess...

00:05:17.376 --> 00:05:18.658
Oh, god.

00:05:23.359 --> 00:05:25.024
I should have protected you.

00:05:25.534 --> 00:05:28.072
I should have told you the truth.

00:05:44.724 --> 00:05:46.103
You okay?

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:47.836
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:05:48.723 --> 00:05:50.115
Another nightmare?

00:05:55.983 --> 00:05:57.744
Want to drive for a while?

00:06:00.246 --> 00:06:03.440
In your whole life, you
never once asked me that.

00:06:03.898 --> 00:06:06.333
Just thought you might
want to. Never mind.

00:06:07.059 --> 00:06:08.154
Look, man,

00:06:08.707 --> 00:06:11.038
You're worried about
me. I get it, and ...

00:06:11.226 --> 00:06:14.934
Thank you, but I'm perfectly okay.

00:06:18.006 --> 00:06:20.415
All right. Where are we?

00:06:20.822 --> 00:06:23.497
We are just outside of Grand Junction.

00:06:27.666 --> 00:06:31.014
You know what? Maybe we shouldn't
have left Stanford so soon.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:35.082
Sam, we dug around there for a
week. We came up with nothing.

00:06:35.446 --> 00:06:39.201
If you want to find the thing that
killed Jessica... Got to find dad first.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.255
Dad disappearing, and this thing
showing up again after 20 years?

00:06:44.494 --> 00:06:46.340
It's no coincidence.

00:06:46.778 --> 00:06:50.157
Dad will have answers. He'll
know what to do. It's weird, man.

00:06:50.517 --> 00:06:53.943
These coordinates he left
us, this Black Water Ridge...

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:56.550
What about it? There's nothing there.

00:06:57.144 --> 00:06:59.621
It's just woods.

00:07:01.357 --> 00:07:04.158
Why is he sending us to
the middle of nowhere?

00:07:11.105 --> 00:07:13.405
So Black Water Ridge is pretty remote.

00:07:13.514 --> 00:07:16.881
It's cut off by these canyons
here --Rough terrain, dense forest,

00:07:16.882 --> 00:07:19.382
Abandoned silver and gold
mines all over the place...

00:07:19.507 --> 00:07:22.797
Dude, check out the size
of this friggin' bear.

00:07:25.332 --> 00:07:28.977
And a dozen or more
grizzlies in the area.

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:31.767
It's no nature hike, that's for sure.

00:07:32.158 --> 00:07:35.897
You boys aren't planning to go out
near Black Water Ridge, by any chance?

00:07:36.163 --> 00:07:41.284
Oh, no, sir. We're environmental-Study majors
from U.C. Boulder-Just working on a paper.

00:07:41.378 --> 00:07:42.926
Recycle, man.

00:07:43.229 --> 00:07:44.371
Bull.

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.954
You're friends with
that Hailey girl, right?

00:07:49.273 --> 00:07:49.899
Yes.

00:07:50.337 --> 00:07:51.901
Yes, we are.

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:54.452
Ranger... Wilkinson.

00:07:55.285 --> 00:07:57.505
Well, I will tell you
exactly what I told her.

00:07:57.506 --> 00:08:02.906
Her brother filled out a backcountry permit saying
he wouldn't be back from Black Water until the 24th.

00:08:03.008 --> 00:08:05.558
So it's not exactly a
missing persons now, is it?

00:08:06.168 --> 00:08:09.250
Tell that girl to quit worrying.
I'm sure her brother's just fine.

00:08:09.407 --> 00:08:10.737
We will.

00:08:11.519 --> 00:08:13.569
Well, that Hailey girl's
quite a pistol, huh?

00:08:13.698 --> 00:08:15.404
That is putting it mildly.

00:08:15.565 --> 00:08:19.969
Actually, you know what would help is if I
could show her a copy of that backcountry permit.

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:23.670
You know, so she could see
her brother's return date.

00:08:24.973 --> 00:08:27.445
Yeah. Heh heh.

00:08:27.586 --> 00:08:29.385
What, are you cruising
for a hookup or something?

00:08:29.447 --> 00:08:30.198
What do you mean?

00:08:30.312 --> 00:08:32.851
The coordinates point to Black Water
Ridge. So what are we waiting for?

00:08:32.852 --> 00:08:36.352
Let's just go find dad.
Why even talk to this girl?

00:08:36.461 --> 00:08:40.669
I don't know, maybe we should know what we're
walking into before we actually walk into it.

00:08:41.591 --> 00:08:42.530
What?

00:08:42.608 --> 00:08:45.910
Since when are you all "shoot
first, ask questions later" anyway?

00:08:46.176 --> 00:08:47.599
Since now.

00:08:49.524 --> 00:08:51.057
Oh, really?

00:08:54.563 --> 00:08:56.159
You must be Hailey Collins.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:09:00.302
I'm Dean, this is Sam. We're rangers with the
park service. Ranger Wilkinson sent us over.

00:09:00.303 --> 00:09:04.003
We wanted to ask you some
questions about your brother Tommy.

00:09:04.941 --> 00:09:06.756
Let me see some I.D.

00:09:09.659 --> 00:09:10.911
There you go.

00:09:17.701 --> 00:09:20.439
Come on in. Thanks.

00:09:21.644 --> 00:09:22.504
That yours?

00:09:22.739 --> 00:09:23.318
Yeah.

00:09:23.459 --> 00:09:24.570
Nice car.

00:09:29.491 --> 00:09:33.324
So, if Tommy's not due back for a
while, how do you know something's wrong?

00:09:33.563 --> 00:09:37.791
He checks in every day by cell. He
e-Mails photos, stupid little videos.

00:09:37.792 --> 00:09:40.292
But we haven't heard anything
in over three days now.

00:09:40.553 --> 00:09:42.493
Well, maybe he can't get cell reception.

00:09:42.795 --> 00:09:44.485
He's got a satellite phone, too.

00:09:44.876 --> 00:09:49.538
Could it be he's just having fun and
forgot to check in? He wouldn't do that.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.944
Our parents are gone. It's
just my two brothers and me.

00:09:53.945 --> 00:09:56.445
We all keep pretty
close tabs on each other.

00:09:57.023 --> 00:09:59.870
Can I see the pictures
he sent you? Yeah.

00:10:00.762 --> 00:10:02.186
That's Tommy.

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:11.544
Hey, Hailey. Day six. We're
still out near Black Water Ridge.

00:10:11.545 --> 00:10:15.545
We're fine, keeping safe, so don't
worry, okay? Talk to you tomorrow.

00:10:17.222 --> 00:10:20.464
We'll find your brother. We're heading
out to Black Water Ridge first thing.

00:10:20.465 --> 00:10:22.965
Then maybe I'll see you there.

00:10:23.918 --> 00:10:24.779
Look.

00:10:24.971 --> 00:10:26.817
I can't sit around here anymore,

00:10:27.052 --> 00:10:30.916
So I hired a guide. I'm heading out in the
morning, and I'm gonna find Tommy myself.

00:10:31.672 --> 00:10:33.951
I think I know how you feel.

00:10:36.084 --> 00:10:38.400
Hey, you mind forwarding these to me?

00:10:38.666 --> 00:10:39.636
Sure.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:47.909
So, Black Water Ridge doesn't get a
lot of traffic-Local campers mostly--

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:52.910
But, still, this past april, two hikers went
missing out there. They were never found.

00:10:52.977 --> 00:10:54.291
Any before that?

00:10:54.369 --> 00:10:54.980
Yeah.

00:10:55.027 --> 00:10:58.067
In 1982, eight different people
all vanished in the same year.

00:10:58.068 --> 00:11:00.268
Authorities said it
was a grizzly attack.

00:11:00.268 --> 00:11:05.468
And, again, in 1959, and
again, before that, in 1936.

00:11:05.577 --> 00:11:08.844
Every 23 years, just like clockwork.

00:11:09.285 --> 00:11:10.804
Okay, watch this.

00:11:11.033 --> 00:11:12.650
Here's the clincher.

00:11:13.538 --> 00:11:18.438
I downloaded that guy Tommy's
video to the laptop. Check this out.

00:11:19.778 --> 00:11:21.264
Do it again.

00:11:24.358 --> 00:11:29.699
That's three frames. It's a fraction of a
second. Whatever that thing is, it can move.

00:11:30.663 --> 00:11:32.999
I told you something weird was going on.

00:11:33.326 --> 00:11:35.972
Yeah. I got one more thing.

00:11:36.098 --> 00:11:41.030
In '59, one camper survived the
supposed grizzly attack, just a kid

00:11:41.227 --> 00:11:43.317
Barely crawled out of the woods alive.

00:11:43.657 --> 00:11:45.065
Is there a name?

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:49.684
Look, ranger, I don't know why
you're asking me about this.

00:11:49.826 --> 00:11:52.673
It's public record. I was a kid.

00:11:52.876 --> 00:11:55.223
My parents got mauled by a... grizzly?

00:11:55.418 --> 00:11:56.904
That's what attacked them?

00:12:05.215 --> 00:12:07.452
The other people that
went missing that year,

00:12:07.656 --> 00:12:09.690
Those bear attacks, too?

00:12:11.928 --> 00:12:14.432
What about all the people
that went missing this year?

00:12:15.151 --> 00:12:16.747
Same thing?

00:12:18.848 --> 00:12:22.990
If we knew what we were dealing
with, we might be able to stop it.

00:12:24.919 --> 00:12:27.547
I seriously doubt that.

00:12:27.954 --> 00:12:29.033
Anyways,

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:32.689
I don't see the
difference it would make.

00:12:33.972 --> 00:12:35.849
You wouldn't believe me.

00:12:36.178 --> 00:12:38.399
Nobody ever did.

00:12:41.135 --> 00:12:42.622
Mr. Shaw

00:12:45.688 --> 00:12:47.565
What did you see?

00:12:52.146 --> 00:12:53.585
Nothing.

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:58.404
It moved too fast to see.

00:12:58.451 --> 00:13:00.062
It hid too well.

00:13:00.176 --> 00:13:01.663
I heard it, though.

00:13:02.257 --> 00:13:04.228
A roar

00:13:05.981 --> 00:13:06.873
Like ...

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:10.526
No man or animal I ever heard.

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:12.619
It came at night?

00:13:13.308 --> 00:13:15.185
Got inside your tent?

00:13:15.503 --> 00:13:17.991
It got inside our cabin.

00:13:18.789 --> 00:13:22.669
I was sleeping in front of
the fireplace when it came in.

00:13:23.315 --> 00:13:26.397
It didn't smash a
window or break the door,

00:13:27.043 --> 00:13:29.062
It unlocked it.

00:13:29.844 --> 00:13:33.693
Do you know of a bear that
could do something like that?

00:13:34.355 --> 00:13:38.188
I didn't even wake up until
I heard my parents screaming.

00:13:38.423 --> 00:13:39.565
It killed them?

00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:41.974
Dragged them off into the night.

00:13:44.508 --> 00:13:49.843
Why it left me alive --I've been
asking myself that ever since.

00:13:54.275 --> 00:13:56.450
It did leave me this, though.

00:14:06.407 --> 00:14:10.271
There's something evil in those woods.

00:14:13.009 --> 00:14:15.403
It was some sort of a demon.

00:14:15.877 --> 00:14:19.401
Spirits and demons don't have to unlock
doors. They just go through the walls.

00:14:19.402 --> 00:14:22.402
So it's probably something
else -Something corporeal.

00:14:22.531 --> 00:14:23.626
"Corporeal"?

00:14:23.892 --> 00:14:25.144
Excuse me, professor.

00:14:25.289 --> 00:14:27.151
Shut up. So, what do you think?

00:14:27.667 --> 00:14:30.108
The claws, the speed that it moves.

00:14:30.436 --> 00:14:32.580
It could be a skinwalker,
maybe a black dog

00:14:32.734 --> 00:14:37.365
Whatever we're talking about, we're talking
about a creature, and it's corporeal,

00:14:37.506 --> 00:14:39.623
Which means we can kill it.

00:14:56.770 --> 00:14:59.023
We cannot let that
Hailey girl go out there.

00:14:59.085 --> 00:15:02.843
Oh yeah, what are we gonna tell her she can't go
into the woods because of a big, scary monster?

00:15:02.844 --> 00:15:04.844
Yeah.

00:15:05.583 --> 00:15:06.929
Her brother's missing, Sam.

00:15:07.132 --> 00:15:08.837
She's not just gonna sit this out.

00:15:09.135 --> 00:15:13.333
No, we go with her, we protect her, and we keep
our eyes peeled for our fuzzy predator friend

00:15:13.427 --> 00:15:15.351
So finding dad's not enough?

00:15:17.749 --> 00:15:19.955
Now we got to babysit, too?

00:15:22.740 --> 00:15:23.726
What?

00:15:25.024 --> 00:15:26.057
Nothing.

00:15:33.091 --> 00:15:36.193
I'll tell you again. I
don't think ben should come.

00:15:36.804 --> 00:15:38.008
Roy...

00:15:38.483 --> 00:15:43.239
Look, you're paying me good money to keep
everybody safe. I think Ben's safest at home.

00:15:53.503 --> 00:15:55.145
You guys got room for two more?

00:15:55.338 --> 00:15:57.012
You want to come with us?

00:15:57.090 --> 00:15:57.998
Who are these guys?

00:15:58.045 --> 00:16:01.409
Apparently, this is all the
park service could muster up.

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:02.775
You're rangers?

00:16:02.822 --> 00:16:03.666
That's right.

00:16:03.823 --> 00:16:06.874
And you're hiking out
in biker boots and jeans?

00:16:08.141 --> 00:16:10.801
Well, sweet heart, I don't do shorts.

00:16:12.767 --> 00:16:17.163
Oh, you think this is funny? It's dangerous
backcountry out there. Her brother might be hurt.

00:16:19.541 --> 00:16:22.091
Believe me, I know how
dangerous it can be.

00:16:22.652 --> 00:16:25.124
We just want to help them
find their brother. That's all.

00:17:23.554 --> 00:17:25.885
Roy, you said you did a little hunting.

00:17:26.156 --> 00:17:28.143
Yeah, more than a little.

00:17:30.052 --> 00:17:31.761
What kind of furry critters do you hunt?

00:17:31.918 --> 00:17:34.405
Mostly buck. Sometimes bear.

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:39.443
Tell me, uh, Bambi or
Yogi ever hunt you back?

00:17:43.456 --> 00:17:45.678
What you doing, Roy?

00:17:51.674 --> 00:17:54.303
You should watch where
you're stepping... ranger.

00:17:58.199 --> 00:18:00.311
It's a bear trap.

00:18:06.423 --> 00:18:08.707
You didn't pack any provisions.

00:18:08.816 --> 00:18:10.646
You guys are carrying a duffel bag.

00:18:10.756 --> 00:18:13.822
You're not rangers, so
who the hell are you?

00:18:22.392 --> 00:18:24.316
Sam and I are brothers,

00:18:24.614 --> 00:18:26.241
And we're looking for our father.

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:27.876
He might be here. We don't know.

00:18:28.016 --> 00:18:30.989
I just figured that you and
me, we're in the same boat.

00:18:32.637 --> 00:18:36.282
Why didn't you just tell me that
from the start? I'm telling you now.

00:18:36.767 --> 00:18:39.850
Besides, it's probably the most
honest I've ever been with a woman...

00:18:40.397 --> 00:18:41.664
Ever.

00:18:43.030 --> 00:18:44.391
So, we okay?

00:18:48.381 --> 00:18:50.196
Yeah, okay.

00:18:50.717 --> 00:18:53.048
And what do you mean I
didn't pack provisions?

00:19:09.827 --> 00:19:11.282
This is it.

00:19:11.689 --> 00:19:12.893
Black Water Ridge.

00:19:12.956 --> 00:19:14.818
What coordinates are we at?

00:19:18.776 --> 00:19:20.987
35 and minus 111.

00:19:26.322 --> 00:19:27.323
You hear that?

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:28.543
Yeah.

00:19:30.149 --> 00:19:31.901
Not even crickets.

00:19:32.668 --> 00:19:34.561
I'm gonna go take a look around.

00:19:34.926 --> 00:19:37.194
You shouldn't go off by yourself.

00:19:37.304 --> 00:19:40.746
That's sweet. Don't worry about me.

00:19:48.836 --> 00:19:52.701
All right, everybody
stays together. Let's go.

00:20:01.379 --> 00:20:03.413
Hailey! Over here!

00:20:11.007 --> 00:20:12.337
Oh, my god.

00:20:12.728 --> 00:20:14.496
Looks like a grizzly.

00:20:31.107 --> 00:20:32.280
Tommy?

00:20:34.079 --> 00:20:35.174
Tommy!

00:20:35.644 --> 00:20:38.151
Tommy! Shh... Shh...

00:20:38.945 --> 00:20:39.899
Why?

00:20:40.337 --> 00:20:41.964
Something might still be out there.

00:20:42.845 --> 00:20:43.878
Sam.

00:20:51.439 --> 00:20:53.931
The bodies were dragged
from the campsite.

00:20:55.042 --> 00:20:58.140
But here, the tracks just vanish.

00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:00.158
It's weird.

00:21:02.317 --> 00:21:04.570
I tell you what.

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:07.590
It's no skinwalker or black dog.

00:21:30.603 --> 00:21:32.981
Hey, he could still be alive.

00:21:36.876 --> 00:21:39.020
Help!

00:22:00.497 --> 00:22:03.329
It seemed like it was coming
from around here, didn't it?

00:22:09.306 --> 00:22:11.496
Everybody back to camp.

00:22:17.511 --> 00:22:19.075
Our packs!

00:22:19.717 --> 00:22:22.752
So much for my GPS
and my satellite phone.

00:22:22.866 --> 00:22:24.227
What the hell's going on?

00:22:24.321 --> 00:22:25.432
It's smart.

00:22:25.510 --> 00:22:27.950
It wants to cut us off
so we can't call for help.

00:22:28.169 --> 00:22:32.284
You mean someone --Some nut job
out there just stole all our gear.

00:22:32.367 --> 00:22:35.730
I need to speak with you... in private.

00:22:44.600 --> 00:22:47.151
Okay, let me see dad's journal.

00:22:52.978 --> 00:22:53.854
All right.

00:22:54.730 --> 00:22:55.794
Check that out.

00:22:56.921 --> 00:22:58.188
Oh, come on.

00:22:58.459 --> 00:23:02.363
Windigos are in the Minnesota woods or Northern
Michigan. I've never even heard of one this far west.

00:23:02.264 --> 00:23:08.364
Think about it, Dean -The claws,
the way it can mimic a human voice.

00:23:08.724 --> 00:23:09.710
Great.

00:23:10.367 --> 00:23:12.370
Well, then this is useless.

00:23:17.063 --> 00:23:19.269
We got to get these people to safety.

00:23:21.345 --> 00:23:24.130
All right, listen up. It's time to go.

00:23:24.412 --> 00:23:27.963
Things have gotten more complicated.

00:23:28.594 --> 00:23:28.985
What?

00:23:29.079 --> 00:23:31.598
Whatever's out there,
I think I can handle it.

00:23:31.660 --> 00:23:36.213
If you shoot this thing, you're just
gonna make it mad. We have to leave now.

00:23:36.244 --> 00:23:39.226
One, you're talking nonsense, two, you're
in no position to give anybody orders.

00:23:39.227 --> 00:23:40.427
Relax.

00:23:40.582 --> 00:23:43.148
We never should have let you come
out in the first place, all right?

00:23:43.227 --> 00:23:44.228
I'm trying to protect you.

00:23:44.306 --> 00:23:45.401
You protect me?

00:23:45.547 --> 00:23:47.751
I was hunting these woods when your
mommy was still kissing you good night.

00:23:47.752 --> 00:23:48.552
Yeah.

00:23:48.645 --> 00:23:51.398
It's a
damn-Near-Perfect hunter.

00:23:51.899 --> 00:23:53.620
It's smarter than you.

00:23:54.094 --> 00:23:59.492
And it's gonna hunt you down and eat you alive
unless we get your stupid sorry ass out of here.

00:23:59.523 --> 00:24:01.479
You know you're crazy, right? Yeah?

00:24:01.651 --> 00:24:04.268
You ever hunt -Chill out.

00:24:04.331 --> 00:24:08.508
Stop! Stop it. Everybody just stop.

00:24:09.295 --> 00:24:10.140
Look.

00:24:10.390 --> 00:24:12.847
Tommy might still be alive.

00:24:13.347 --> 00:24:15.913
And I'm not leaving here without him.

00:24:20.379 --> 00:24:22.491
It's getting late.

00:24:23.602 --> 00:24:26.027
This thing is a good hunter in the day,

00:24:26.637 --> 00:24:29.000
But an unbelievable hunter at night.

00:24:29.474 --> 00:24:31.758
We'll never beat it
--Not in the dark.

00:24:33.807 --> 00:24:36.154
We need to settle
inand protect ourselves.

00:24:37.140 --> 00:24:38.908
How?

00:24:48.407 --> 00:24:51.630
One more time.That's...?
Anasazi symbols.

00:24:51.786 --> 00:24:55.525
It's for protection. The
windigo can't cross over them.

00:24:56.453 --> 00:24:58.940
Nobody likes a skeptic, Roy.

00:25:09.354 --> 00:25:12.483
You want to tell me what's going
on in that freaky head of yours?

00:25:14.215 --> 00:25:16.296
Dean... No, you're not fine.

00:25:16.984 --> 00:25:19.503
You're like a powder keg,
man. It's not like you.

00:25:20.176 --> 00:25:22.867
I'm supposed to be the
belligerent one, remember?

00:25:26.881 --> 00:25:28.618
Dad's not here.

00:25:31.012 --> 00:25:36.555
I mean, that much we know for sure, right? He
would have left us a message, a sign, right?

00:25:37.447 --> 00:25:39.262
Yeah, you're probably right.

00:25:40.565 --> 00:25:43.381
To tell you the truth, I don't
think dad's ever been to Lost Creek.

00:25:45.211 --> 00:25:48.497
Then let's get these people back
to town, and let's hit the road...

00:25:48.768 --> 00:25:52.507
Go find dad. I mean, why
are we still even here?

00:26:01.175 --> 00:26:02.676
This is why...

00:26:03.099 --> 00:26:04.961
This book.

00:26:05.399 --> 00:26:10.692
This is dad's single most valuable possession.
Everything he knows about every evil thing is in here.

00:26:10.786 --> 00:26:13.070
And he's passed it on to us.

00:26:13.873 --> 00:26:16.689
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:26:17.675 --> 00:26:20.538
You know, saving
people, hunting things...

00:26:20.804 --> 00:26:23.057
The family business.

00:26:25.617 --> 00:26:27.072
That makes no sense.

00:26:27.229 --> 00:26:34.410
Why-Why doesn't he just call us? Why doesn't
he tell us what he wants, tell us where he is?

00:26:35.694 --> 00:26:37.321
I don't know.

00:26:39.011 --> 00:26:40.560
But the way I see it,

00:26:41.921 --> 00:26:45.144
Dad's given us a job to
do, and I intend to do it.

00:26:45.504 --> 00:26:46.834
Dean...

00:26:47.569 --> 00:26:48.461
No.

00:26:49.603 --> 00:26:51.214
I gotta find dad.

00:26:52.028 --> 00:26:54.031
I gotta find Jessica's killer.

00:26:59.953 --> 00:27:05.210
It's the only thing I can think about. Okay.
All right. Sam, we'll find them. I promise.

00:27:06.540 --> 00:27:07.718
Listen to me.

00:27:07.890 --> 00:27:10.018
You've got to prepare yourself.

00:27:10.925 --> 00:27:13.116
I mean, this search could take a while.

00:27:13.872 --> 00:27:15.578
And all that anger,

00:27:15.781 --> 00:27:19.364
You can't keep it burning over
the long haul. It's gonna kill you.

00:27:20.370 --> 00:27:22.310
You got to have patience, man.

00:27:24.848 --> 00:27:26.459
How do you do it?

00:27:27.257 --> 00:27:29.494
How does dad do it?

00:27:30.887 --> 00:27:33.202
Well, for one, them.

00:27:33.911 --> 00:27:38.135
I mean, I figure our family's so screwed
to hell, maybe we can help some others.

00:27:38.437 --> 00:27:40.721
It makes things a
little bit more bearable.

00:27:45.831 --> 00:27:47.881
And I'll tell you what else helps...

00:27:50.212 --> 00:27:54.155
Killing as many evil sons
of bitches as I possibly can.

00:27:56.796 --> 00:27:58.392
Help me!

00:28:01.583 --> 00:28:02.897
Please...!

00:28:07.208 --> 00:28:08.538
Help!

00:28:09.883 --> 00:28:11.401
It's trying to draw us out.

00:28:11.679 --> 00:28:13.135
Just stay cool. Stay put.

00:28:13.267 --> 00:28:15.306
Inside the magic circle?

00:28:15.395 --> 00:28:17.131
Help!

00:28:18.622 --> 00:28:20.187
Help me!

00:28:22.612 --> 00:28:24.614
Okay, that's no grizzly.

00:28:30.082 --> 00:28:33.179
It's okay. We'll be
all right. I promise.

00:28:36.688 --> 00:28:38.613
It's here.

00:28:45.142 --> 00:28:46.315
I hit it!

00:28:46.362 --> 00:28:47.395
Roy, no!

00:28:47.926 --> 00:28:49.053
Roy!

00:28:49.663 --> 00:28:51.024
Don't move.

00:28:55.284 --> 00:28:58.162
It's over here. Ugh!

00:28:59.795 --> 00:29:00.827
Roy?!

00:29:27.572 --> 00:29:28.621
I don't...

00:29:29.090 --> 00:29:32.078
I mean, these types of things--
They aren't supposed to be real.

00:29:32.313 --> 00:29:34.018
I wish I could tell you different.

00:29:35.228 --> 00:29:37.277
How do we know it's not
out there watching us?

00:29:37.809 --> 00:29:38.967
We don't.

00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:41.569
But we're safe for now.

00:29:42.993 --> 00:29:44.839
How do you know about this stuff?

00:29:47.405 --> 00:29:49.189
It kind of runs in the family.

00:29:54.871 --> 00:29:55.888
Hey.

00:29:56.983 --> 00:30:00.019
So, we've got half a
chance in the daylight.

00:30:00.320 --> 00:30:02.620
And I, for one...

00:30:03.105 --> 00:30:05.593
Want to kill this evil son of a bitch.

00:30:06.474 --> 00:30:08.351
Well, hell, you know I'm in.

00:30:08.763 --> 00:30:11.684
Windigo is a cree indian word.
It means, "evil that devours."

00:30:11.685 --> 00:30:13.285
They're hundreds of years old.

00:30:13.347 --> 00:30:19.625
Each one was once a man, sometimes an indian or
other times a frontiers manor a miner or hunter.

00:30:19.771 --> 00:30:22.931
How's a man turn into one of those
things? Well, it's always the same.

00:30:23.041 --> 00:30:24.449
During some harsh winter,

00:30:24.590 --> 00:30:27.985
A guy finds himself starving,
cut off from supplies or help

00:30:28.225 --> 00:30:32.793
Becomes a cannibal to survive, eating
other members of his tribe or camp.

00:30:32.871 --> 00:30:34.780
Like the donner party.

00:30:35.524 --> 00:30:39.298
Cultures all over the world believe that eating
human flesh gives a person certain abilities--

00:30:39.299 --> 00:30:42.299
Speed, strength, immortality.

00:30:42.383 --> 00:30:43.897
If you eat enough of it,

00:30:44.100 --> 00:30:46.385
Over years, you become this ...

00:30:46.588 --> 00:30:48.966
Less-Than-Human
thing.

00:30:49.129 --> 00:30:51.006
You're always hungry.

00:30:51.100 --> 00:30:54.949
So, if that's true, how
can Tommy still be alive?

00:30:57.124 --> 00:30:59.241
You're not gonna like it. Tell me.

00:30:59.569 --> 00:31:02.964
More than anything, a windigo knows
how to last long winters without food.

00:31:03.047 --> 00:31:06.082
It hibernates for years
at a time. When it's awake,

00:31:06.489 --> 00:31:09.654
It keeps its victims
alive. It stores them

00:31:09.983 --> 00:31:12.329
So it can feed whenever it wants.

00:31:13.456 --> 00:31:18.655
If your brother's alive, it's keeping
him somewhere dark, hidden, and safe

00:31:19.312 --> 00:31:21.158
And we got to track it back there.

00:31:21.299 --> 00:31:23.213
And then how do we stop it?

00:31:23.322 --> 00:31:24.402
Well,

00:31:24.668 --> 00:31:27.734
Guns are useless-So are knives.

00:31:28.756 --> 00:31:30.414
Basically...

00:31:30.821 --> 00:31:33.700
We gotta torch the sucker.

00:31:49.964 --> 00:31:50.981
Dean.

00:31:54.173 --> 00:31:55.299
What is it?

00:32:13.348 --> 00:32:14.615
You know,

00:32:14.960 --> 00:32:19.153
I was thinking that those claw
prints, so clear and distinct

00:32:20.800 --> 00:32:23.178
They were almost too easy to follow.

00:32:49.262 --> 00:32:53.000
You okay? His neck's broken.

00:32:53.736 --> 00:32:56.526
Run, run! Go, go, go, go, go!

00:33:05.696 --> 00:33:08.856
Come on. I got you. I got you.

00:33:18.740 --> 00:33:20.102
Hailey!

00:33:30.114 --> 00:33:31.428
Dean!

00:33:32.935 --> 00:33:36.517
If it keeps its victims
alive, why would it kill Roy?

00:33:36.721 --> 00:33:37.753
Honestly?

00:33:38.129 --> 00:33:41.274
I think because Roy shot
at it, he pissed it off.

00:33:48.883 --> 00:33:50.448
They went this way.

00:33:56.352 --> 00:33:58.495
It's better than bread crumbs.

00:35:40.674 --> 00:35:44.648
Hey, it's okay. It's okay. It's okay.

00:35:57.001 --> 00:35:58.159
Dean.

00:36:00.474 --> 00:36:01.945
You. Wake up.

00:36:02.810 --> 00:36:05.297
Dean. Hey. You okay?

00:36:07.863 --> 00:36:08.958
Yeah.

00:36:09.245 --> 00:36:11.529
Hailey... Hailey.

00:36:11.826 --> 00:36:13.923
Wake up. Wake up.

00:36:15.127 --> 00:36:16.270
Gotcha.

00:36:26.442 --> 00:36:29.431
You sure you're all right?
Yeah, yeah. Where is it?

00:36:29.530 --> 00:36:31.376
It's gone for now.

00:36:52.081 --> 00:36:52.957
Tommy.

00:36:56.477 --> 00:36:57.260
Tommy.

00:37:03.434 --> 00:37:05.030
Cut him down.

00:37:18.591 --> 00:37:20.375
We're gonna get you home.

00:37:21.287 --> 00:37:22.695
Check it out.

00:37:23.513 --> 00:37:26.048
Flare guns. Those will work.

00:37:40.500 --> 00:37:44.678
Looks like someone's home for
supper. We'll never out run it.

00:37:48.730 --> 00:37:51.202
You thinking what I'm
thinking? Yeah, I think so.

00:37:54.633 --> 00:37:57.251
All right, listen to me. Stay with
Sam. He's gonna get you out of here.

00:37:57.252 --> 00:37:58.952
What are you gonna do?

00:38:01.569 --> 00:38:04.244
It's chow time, you freakin' bastard!

00:38:04.573 --> 00:38:08.828
Yeah, that's right! Bring
it on, baby! I taste good!

00:38:16.799 --> 00:38:19.005
All right, come on. Hurry!

00:38:24.272 --> 00:38:25.508
Hey!

00:38:26.729 --> 00:38:28.997
Hey, you want some white meat, bitch?!

00:38:29.185 --> 00:38:30.515
I'm right here!

00:38:46.066 --> 00:38:47.680
Get him out of here. Sam, no.

00:38:47.681 --> 00:38:49.681
Go. Go!

00:38:50.071 --> 00:38:50.712
Go.

00:39:00.128 --> 00:39:01.067
Come on.

00:39:02.458 --> 00:39:03.413
Come on.

00:39:18.571 --> 00:39:19.447
Sam!

00:39:21.439 --> 00:39:24.552
Come on. Hurry, hurry, hurry! Go!

00:39:37.334 --> 00:39:38.836
Get behind me.

00:40:21.915 --> 00:40:24.199
Not bad, huh?

00:40:32.355 --> 00:40:37.643
That's when it circled the campsite. I mean,
this grizzly must have weighed 800, 900 pounds.

00:40:39.494 --> 00:40:42.779
So, really, I don't
know how to thank you.

00:40:45.960 --> 00:40:49.559
Must you cheapen the moment? Yeah!

00:40:50.588 --> 00:40:53.655
You riding with your brother? Yeah.

00:40:55.235 --> 00:40:56.299
Let's go.

00:41:08.375 --> 00:41:10.628
I hope you find your father.

00:41:13.971 --> 00:41:15.457
Thanks, Sam.

00:41:33.159 --> 00:41:35.458
Man, I hate camping.

00:41:35.771 --> 00:41:37.007
Me too.

00:41:40.172 --> 00:41:42.394
Sam, you know we're
gonna find dad, right?

00:41:43.317 --> 00:41:45.382
Yeah, I know.

00:41:46.795 --> 00:41:49.017
But in the meantime

00:41:50.769 --> 00:41:52.537
I'm driving.



00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.000
